From c1b9b3bd2235281ae5212a42d8459570ced60407 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tran Ha Tam <tranhatam@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Apr 2026 18:20:46 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] mail-api(path-b): in-package bootstrap entrypoint +
 env-driven sink config

Replace the ad-hoc bootstrap.mjs deployed during the 2026-04-28 Path B
rollout with a first-class entrypoint living inside @iai/mail-api.

- src/bootstrap.ts: pure buildServerOptionsFromEnv() + Promise-wrapped
  bootstrapFromEnv() + CLI shim guarded by import.meta.url. Emits a
  single JSON line on listen / failure for log scrapers.
- src/inbound-webhook.ts: resolveInboundWebhookOptionsFromEnv() reads
  MAIL_API_INBOUND_EVIDENCE_FILE / _REPLAY_WINDOW_S / _MAX_BODY_BYTES,
  picks file vs in-memory sink, throws on bad integers.
- package.json: add bin 'iai-mail-api' and './bootstrap' subpath export.
- tests/integration/mail-api-bootstrap.test.mjs: 8/8 cover env branches,
  PORT=0 ephemeral, legacy alias, and restart-safe persistence (one
  bootstrap writes evidence, a second bootstrap reads it back).

Operationally inert: live VPS container keeps running the previous
bootstrap.mjs; next image rebuild should switch CMD to
node ./dist/bootstrap.js. Docs PATH_B_STATUS / DEPLOY_COMPLETE updated
to point at the canonical codepath. Full mail-api integration suite
21/21 pass; typecheck + build clean.
